"""Silverpine South: the outer direction the old accept line used to give."""

STORY = {
    'sps_pond_edge': ("Right, here's what I actually think, and you're the first person I've said it to, because the March haven't the time and the Apothecaries would want it in writing.\n\nThe pond is draining, slowly, a hand's width a season, maybe, and it's been doing it since before the oozes started. I've got marks on three stones to prove it.\n\nAnd here's the part I like less. The water's going somewhere, and something's coming the other way. Whatever rises in that pond isn't drowning in it, it's arriving.\n\nWalk the whole edge for me. I don't mean my circuit. I mean the whole edge, the far side included, and tell me where the ground is wet that shouldn't be and dry that shouldn't be. Olivia's Pond is west of here, and the far bank is the west one.", None),
    'sps_bloated_one': ("I've found the source. It's been in the middle of my pond the whole time, and I walked past it every day for two years thinking it was a sunken log.\n\nThere's a corpse at the heart of the water so swollen it can't rise any more. It just lies there and lashes at whatever comes near, and everything that bursts off it goes into the water and comes out of the water as something else.\n\nThat's the gas, that's the oozes, that's the whole business.\n\nIt'll burst when you hit it. I want you going in knowing that, because whatever bursts out will be worse than what was lying there. Finish it anyway. Olivia's Pond is just west of here.", None),
    'sps_bloodmaw': ("Bloodmaw is the reason the Peril holds.\n\nHe's grey-muzzled, old, and he's outlived every single challenger, and in a pack that advertises its rank in teeth you can read exactly how many on the collar he wears. He's got a scar the length of his flank that somebody earned and didn't survive collecting.\n\nI want you to understand what he actually is, because alpha makes it sound like he's just the biggest. He isn't the biggest any more. He's the one who taught them the line, and the packmasters are his. Every one of those strings you brought me came off a wolf he trained.\n\nTake him, and the Peril stops being a succession and goes back to being wolves. Beren's Peril is south of here.", None),
    'sps_wall_seals': ("There's something the Wall Guard carry, and I'd like it off them before anybody else thinks of it.\n\nThey carry the seals they swore their oaths on. Every Gilnean guardsman had one, and they went into the wall with them, and they're still holding them.\n\nThe Forsaken relief comes down the Wall road next month. Somebody in that column is going to look at a row of ghosts holding Gilnean seals and see salvage, and I'd very much like the seals to be somewhere else by then.\n\nI'm going to lay them on the shut gate, all of them, on the step, where they'd have been laid if there'd been anybody left to do it properly. Then whatever the relief does, that part will already have been done right. The Greymane Wall is south of here.", None),
    'sps_shut_gate': ("I want you to go and look at the gate itself, properly, up close, and I'll tell you why in a moment.\n\nThat gate hasn't opened since the night Gilneas shut itself off. There hasn't been a crack, or a hinge-shift, nothing, and I've got the detail's log going back to before I took it, and every corporal has written the same word in it every night.\n\nHere's my trouble. I've been writing that word for eleven months, and about a month ago I realised I'd stopped actually looking before I wrote it. You get into the habit of a thing being true.\n\nSo go and look, and come back and tell me what you see rather than what the log says. If it's still shut, I'd like to have been told so by somebody who checked. The Greymane Wall gate is south-east of here.", None),
    'sps_sfk_pickets': ("Marl has the days on the Shadowfang gate and I've got the nights, and the road past the pickets is the worst of both. The ghouls and the stalkers crowd it, and they aren't coming down it. They're pressed up against it, facing the keep, as if something inside were calling them.\n\nThere's a party going in soon, and I'd rather they spent what they've got inside instead of on the way up.\n\nClear the Rotting Ghouls and the Feral Worgen Stalkers off the keep road. The keep road runs south past Beren's Peril.", None),
    'sps_sfk_forecourt': ("I want to ask you something, and I want an honest answer rather than a kind one.\n\nI've stood at that gate for years. The howling comes down out of that keep every night, and it's never once stopped.\n\nAnd I can't tell you any more whether it's got louder, or whether I've simply got used to it and lost my measure. Those are very different facts, and I've no way to tell them apart from the gate, because the only instrument I had was me, and I've been standing in it too long.\n\nGo and stand in the forecourt. Don't go inside, just the forecourt. Listen to it with ears that haven't heard it before, and then come back and tell me straight. The forecourt of Shadowfang Keep is a long way south of here.", None),
}
STORY['sps_deserters'] = ("Now something I'd rather not be asking a stranger to do.\n\nSome of the March walked off. It wasn't a rout or a panic. They simply stopped, and left, and went up to the Bucklebree farm and set themselves up as brigands on it.\n\nThey did it under my nose. I'd like that on the record. I've been round it a hundred times and I can't find the morning where I'd have done differently, and it still happened on my watch and in my sight.\n\nThey're robbing carters on my road now, which makes them my problem twice over. Deal with the Field Deserters. I'm not asking you to do anything I wouldn't. I'm asking because a sergeant going up there personally becomes a story, and this is bad enough without being a story.", None)
